# MERGE RULES FOR THE UPSTREAM SYNC — see CLAUDE.md, "This dashboard is a downstream of Sattva".
#
# `.github/workflows/sync-upstream.yml` merges techmuns/Sattva-Central-Research into this repository
# on a schedule. Files marked `merge=ours` keep THIS repository's version whenever both sides changed
# them, so a merge never conflicts on them. The driver is a no-op (`git config merge.ours.driver true`),
# which the workflow sets before merging; a local merge needs the same one-line config or git falls
# back to the normal three-way merge for these paths.
#
# WHAT QUALIFIES: only files that are GENERATED here, by this repository's own scheduled scrapes or by
# a build step, and that describe THIS deployment's book and universe. A hand-written source file must
# never be listed — a code file marked `ours` would silently discard every upstream fix to it.

# Committed data captures. Both repositories regenerate these daily from their own book and universe;
# taking upstream's copy would paint another deployment's portfolio here. A file only upstream changed
# still arrives (the driver applies only when both sides changed it), and the next scheduled run here
# rewrites it with this deployment's own capture.
public/data/*.json           merge=ours
public/data/mock/*.json      merge=ours

# The generated stylesheet. Rebuilt from tailwind.config.cjs (which carries this deployment's palette)
# after every merge, so whatever the merge did to it is overwritten anyway.
public/css/tailwind.css      merge=ours
